source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: The hidden `}}` stays inside the body and the span closes at the later one, and the pair inside that body is its token's last run, so Jira renders a forced newline there; jiro pairs the same braces, keeps both backslashes as code and warns.
-- input.jira --
{{a\\}}b}}
-- rendered.html --
<p><tt>a<br class="atl-forced-newline" />}}b</tt></p>
-- want.md --
`a\\}}b`
-- warnings.json --
[
  {
    "Line": 1,
    "Column": 1,
    "Construct": "inline-code",
    "Reason": "Jira would render a forced newline inside this Monospace Span; inline code keeps the characters literal"
  }
]
